\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Behaviour of the simulated techniques as the context length grows at \texttt  {batch=1}. \textbf  {Left:} peak GPU memory versus context length; the GQA curve is the lowest among the architectural techniques, while MiniKV and xKV reach the lowest absolute cache sizes. \textbf  {Centre:} throughput in tokens per second; quantization preserves the FP16 throughput baseline while compression and eviction add small overheads. \textbf  {Right:} per-token latency on a log scale; PagedAttention and the baseline dominate the low-latency region, while CPU Offloading pays a fixed transfer cost per generated token.}}{8}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:context_curves}{{2}{8}{Behaviour of the simulated techniques as the context length grows at \texttt {batch=1}. \textbf {Left:} peak GPU memory versus context length; the GQA curve is the lowest among the architectural techniques, while MiniKV and xKV reach the lowest absolute cache sizes. \textbf {Centre:} throughput in tokens per second; quantization preserves the FP16 throughput baseline while compression and eviction add small overheads. \textbf {Right:} per-token latency on a log scale; PagedAttention and the baseline dominate the low-latency region, while CPU Offloading pays a fixed transfer cost per generated token}{figure.2}{}}
